course: dictionary
lesson: 3637
title: Finished: done, complete, at the end
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Finished means done. When a job is complete, nothing more needs doing, so it is finished. «The finished poster was handed in late» means the poster was complete, even though it arrived after the deadline.
explain: Finished is also the past of finish. «She finishes her sums» happens now, but «She finished her sums» happened earlier. Adding -ed to finish shows that the work is already done.
explain: Context helps again. «I'm finished» can mean I have nothing more to do, or that I have eaten all I want. Read the words around it: at a dinner table it means you are full, and at school it means your work is done.
fact: Finished means done, at the end, or complete.
fact: Finished is the past of the verb finish: finish, finishes, finished, finishing.
fact: «I'm finished» can mean I have nothing more to do or eat.
fact: In maths, left = total − finished: if 24 pupils are in a class and 15 have finished, then 9 are left.
fact: A quick check: swap in «done» or «complete» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The finished poster was handed in late.» What does finished mean here? | Torn in half | Hidden away | Still being drawn | *Complete and done
exercise: A class has 24 pupils. 15 have finished their maths. How many are still left to finish? | *9 | 39 | 24 | 15
exercise: Which word is the past of finish? | finishes | finishing | finish | *finished
test: Tom says «I'm finished!» at the dinner table. What does he most likely mean? | He has just sat down to a big lunch | *He has eaten all he wants | He has lost his plate | He is going to start cooking
test: «The Great Pyramid of Giza was finished about 2560 BC.» What does finished tell us? | It was lost in 2560 | It was going to be built soon | It was painted in the year 2560 | *It was completed around 2560 BC
exam: Which word means the same as finished in «a finished car drives out of the factory»? | Broken | Missing | Hungry | *Complete
